WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.640
Hi. This is Matt Baker. Recently I did a pair&nbsp;
of videos on the words Israel and Palestine and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.200
how each of these words can mean different&nbsp;
things, depending on the context. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:17.200
two words that I didn't go into much detail on&nbsp;
(even though they obviously came up) were Zionism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:23.440
and Anti-Zionism. So I figured a third video&nbsp;
was needed in order to clear a few things up.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:29.200
First off, in the Israel video, I made it seem as&nbsp;
if Anti-Zionism was simply being critical of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.840
actions of the current Israeli government.&nbsp;
But this is actually not the case because,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.760
as several people pointed out in the comments,&nbsp;
many Zionists also oppose the actions of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.800
current Israeli government. In other words I&nbsp;
didn't really get to the heart of the difference&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.720
between Zionists and Anti-Zionists. So&nbsp;
that’s what I’m going to do right now.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:56.080
Let me start by sharing a very basic&nbsp;
definition of Zionism. At its core,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:04.400
Zionism is simply: Support for the continued&nbsp;
existence of Israel as a Jewish state. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.360
regardless of what you think about what is&nbsp;
happening in Gaza and regardless of whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.880
or not you think Palestinians deserve their own&nbsp;
state, if you think Israel should continue to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:20.880
exist as it does right now (meaning as a&nbsp;
country with a uniquely Jewish identity),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:27.840
then you are a Zionist. Now, within this broad&nbsp;
definition, Zionism can obviously take a multitude&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.920
of different forms. Let me describe at least&nbsp;
two, starting with the most extreme version.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:41.280
There are some Zionists who are undeniably&nbsp;
racist and Islamophobic towards Palestinians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.640
who have participated in genocidal war&nbsp;
crimes against them, and who have supported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.200
illegal settlements in Palestinian&nbsp;
areas. This brand of Zionist would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:58.480
like to see Gaza and the West Bank cleared of&nbsp;
all Arabs so that Israel could look like this.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:05.440
However, there are also other Zionists (often&nbsp;
called Liberal Zionists) who strongly oppose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:11.840
the War on Gaza and who even acknowledge that&nbsp;
a genocide has occurred there. These Zionists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:18.480
want Palestinians to have freedom, safety, and&nbsp;
peace but see some sort of a two-state solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:24.080
as the best way forward. Because a two-state&nbsp;
solution would involve the continued existence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:31.040
of Israel as a Jewish state alongside a new,&nbsp;
fully independent Palestinian state, anyone who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:37.840
favors a two-state solution (even if they are&nbsp;
a Palestinian) is, by definition, a Zionist.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.880
Okay, let’s now take a look at Anti-Zionism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:48.640
starting with its most extreme form. There are&nbsp;
some Anti-Zionists who are undeniably antisemitic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.600
hating both the Jewish people as a whole as&nbsp;
well as the State of Israel. They tend to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:59.280
use the same tropes against Israel that have been&nbsp;
used against Jews for centuries and would like to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:05.680
see the Middle East completely cleared of all&nbsp;
Jews so that Palestine would look like this.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:13.040
However, there are also other Anti-Zionists&nbsp;
(including Anti-Zionist Jews) who simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:20.160
see Zionism as a bad idea because it’s deeply&nbsp;
rooted in 19th century ideas about nationalism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:27.840
which are now outdated. This type of Anti-Zionism&nbsp;
acknowledges that the Zionist project (even if its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:34.000
aims were good) necessitated the expulsion of&nbsp;
Palestinians and continues to necessitate their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:40.240
occupation and denial of rights (which is not&nbsp;
good). But here's the part that I really want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:45.440
to highlight. These Anti-Zionists don't want&nbsp;
to make things right by kicking out all of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:51.520
Israeli Jews. No, they want the Israeli Jews to&nbsp;
continue to live safely where they do right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.960
with all their rights and freedoms. The only&nbsp;
difference is that they want the Palestinians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:04.080
to also share in those same rights and freedoms.&nbsp;
And in order for that to make happen, they see a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:10.880
one-state solution as the best way forward—a&nbsp;
state that would be equally Jewish and Arab.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:17.520
So, because this sort of one-state solution would&nbsp;
involve a state that wouldn’t be explicitly just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:24.880
Jewish, anyone who favors a one-state solution&nbsp;
like this is, by definition, an Anti-Zionist.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:32.480
So, I still stand by my earlier statement that&nbsp;
Anti-Zionism doesn't have to be antisemitic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:37.920
just like Zionism doesn't have to be&nbsp;
anti-Palestinian. In my experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:45.360
there are folks in both this camp as well as in&nbsp;
this camp who care deeply about both Jews and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:51.760
Arabs and simply want a solution that can be&nbsp;
good for everyone. Even though we tend to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:58.960
things in terms of this entire side against this&nbsp;
entire side, I think there’s an argument to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:04.720
made that the two positions in the middle actually&nbsp;
have more in common with each other than they do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:12.320
with the extreme versions of themselves (in that&nbsp;
they both want safety and freedom for everyone).&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:17.920
The main disagreement is just over whether a&nbsp;
two-state solution would be better or whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:23.840
a one-state solution would be better. Some&nbsp;
people think a one-state solution would never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:30.160
work and is incredibly naive. Well, there are&nbsp;
others who think a two-state solution would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:36.320
never work and is incredibly naive. Which is&nbsp;
why there are also a lot of people who don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:42.720
even argue for one or the other—they just&nbsp;
want peace and are willing to consider both.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:48.560
The other mistake I made in my first video&nbsp;
was that I said Zionists were a subset of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:54.800
Jews. What I was trying to convey was that,&nbsp;
when Zionism first arose in the late 1800s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:01.520
not all Jews supported it. In fact, up until the&nbsp;
end of World War II, most Jews did not support&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:07.280
it. But here’s the thing. If we fast forward&nbsp;
to today, the vast majority of Zionists are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:14.160
not even Jews at all. They are Christians, mostly&nbsp;
American Christians. And this is something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:20.480
Anti-Zionists point out as being problematic. You&nbsp;
see, according to a certain brand of evangelical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:26.560
Christianity, the Bible is interpreted as saying&nbsp;
that the Jewish People must be returned to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:33.520
homeland—and until this fully happens, Jesus&nbsp;
will not return. So that’s less about supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:39.280
Jewish interests than it is about supporting&nbsp;
their own. And I won't even go into all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:45.600
money that US weapons manufacturers make off&nbsp;
of supporting Zionism. Cogito did a really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:50.560
good video about that—which I'll link to in the&nbsp;
description—if you want to learn more about it.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:55.760
Instead I want to end by pointing out&nbsp;
that it's not just Anti-Zionism that can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:02.400
be antisemitic. Zionism can be too. For&nbsp;
example, in the early days of Zionism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:07.600
a lot of Europeans supported it because they&nbsp;
didn’t want Jews in their own countries. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:13.680
unfortunately this line of thinking still exists&nbsp;
to this day. There are also many Zionists who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:19.120
look negatively upon the long history of Jews&nbsp;
in the diaspora and are embarrassed by it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:25.840
which is a form of internalized antisemitism. In&nbsp;
contrast, many Jewish Anti-Zionists argue that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:31.280
Jews have a rich history in the diaspora—one&nbsp;
that should be celebrated—and that it’s better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:37.680
to fight antisemitism wherever its found rather&nbsp;
than try to avoid it by having a Jewish state.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:43.920
So that was a better look at the terms Zionism&nbsp;
and Anti-Zionism. If you found this series of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:49.200
videos at all helpful and would like to do&nbsp;
something to support those suffering in Gaza,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:54.080
I encourage you to donate to an&nbsp;
organization called Connecting Gaza,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.080 --> 00:08:00.000
a small grassroots organization run by a friend&nbsp;
of mine which is helping people on the ground in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.560
Gaza through personal connections. You can find&nbsp;
the link in the description and pinned comment.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.760
Thanks for watching.

